<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  The Cloudflare tunnel as a user LaunchAgent. cloudflared can drop its edge
  connection while the process still lives (Error 1033 with nothing crashed) —
  KeepAlive alone won't catch that, but RunAtLoad + KeepAlive at least survive
  sleep/reboot/crash, which a hand-started `cloudflared tunnel run` does not.
  Generated from this template by ops/install-services.sh.

  `--protocol http2` is the answer to the 1033 above, and it was earned. Captured
  from tunnel.log while a user was staring at an Error 1033 page:

    11:47:40Z ERR Failed to dial a quic connection — "timeout: no recent network activity"
    11:47:49Z INF Retrying connection in up to 8s
    11:48:08Z ERR failed to serve tunnel connection … Retrying in up to 16s
    11:48:18Z INF Registered tunnel connection connIndex=0
    11:48:31Z INF Registered tunnel connection connIndex=1,2,3

  All four edge connections died together on a UDP timeout and took 38 seconds
  to come back, backing off 4→8→16s. The process never exited, so KeepAlive had
  nothing to restart and doctor reported everything healthy. For that whole
  window the hostname simply does not resolve, which is exactly Error 1033.

  cloudflared defaults to QUIC (UDP). "no recent network activity" is what a
  path that drops or NAT-times-out UDP looks like from the inside. http2 rides
  TCP/443, which is the thing that survives hostile networks — the same reason
  deckhand tunnels HTTP rather than using WebRTC for video. QUIC's lower latency
  is not worth a link that vanishes for half a minute at a time.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key>
  <string>no.deckhand.tunnel</string>
  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>__CLOUDFLARED__</string>
    <string>tunnel</string>
    <string>--protocol</string>
    <string>http2</string>
    <string>run</string>
    <string>__TUNNEL_ID__</string>
  </array>
  <key>RunAtLoad</key>
  <true/>
  <key>KeepAlive</key>
  <true/>
  <key>ThrottleInterval</key>
  <integer>5</integer>
  <key>StandardOutPath</key>
  <string>__LOG_DIR__/tunnel.log</string>
  <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
  <string>__LOG_DIR__/tunnel.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
